    "title": {
     "en": "Guess then check"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Before pouring, guess how many cups will fill a jug. Then check."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "estimate",
     "guess",
     "close",
     "check"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Estimating means a thoughtful guess that is close to the real amount.\nGuess how many cups will fill a jug, then pour and count to check.\nGuess which bag of vegetables is heavier, then check on a balance.\nEvery time you check, your guesses get better.\nEstimate with things you know: a 1 litre bottle holds about 4 big glasses of water.\nRemember to say your estimate with the unit, like about 2 litres."
    }
